($t$Entandrophragma angolense$t$, $t$Entandrophragma angolense$t$, $t$Meliaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Meliaceae. Portamento: Tree. Altezza massima indicativa: 50 m. Entandrophragma angolense or commonly known as Tiama Mahogany is a tropical, deciduous buttressed tree growing up to 50 m in height with 5 m trunk diameter. It has an open crown and smooth, pale grey bark that flakes off. The flowers are white to yellow in colour. The fruit is a capsule. The bark is used medicinally against fever, stomach pain, peptic ulcers, ear ache, arthritic or rheumatic pain, swellings, ophthalmia, etc. The tree is often planted as shade tree in banana, coffee and tea plantations. The wood is light, moderately soft, moderately durable, and resistant to dry wood borers. It is suitable for veneer production and is highly valued for light construction, musical instruments, toys, boxes, crates, and novelties among others. It can also be used as firewood and for charcoal production.$t$, $j${"luce": "Tollera: pieno sole, mezz'ombra", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Tiama Mahogany$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Meliaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semina": [], "finestra_trapianto